**3. INCREASE THE MAXIMUM CAMERA ZOOM-OUT RANGE**

Increase the maximum distance at which the player can zoom out the camera.

The current camera zoom-out limit restricts the player's ability to see the wider battlefield, especially during large engagements involving several squadmates, enemies, and bosses.

Extend the maximum zoom-out distance considerably so players can obtain a broader tactical overview of the battlefield.

The player should be able to:
- See more of the surrounding environment.
- Monitor all five squadmates more easily.
- Observe enemy formations.
- Understand where bosses are positioned.
- Track large-scale engagements.
- Make better tactical decisions.
- Observe battles involving multiple units simultaneously.

The additional zoom range should feel natural and should not make the camera controls uncomfortable.

**Camera behavior:**

Preserve the existing zoom controls and camera movement behavior.

Improve the maximum zoom-out distance without breaking:
- Normal zoom levels.
- Minimum zoom distance.
- Camera rotation.
- Camera positioning.
- Camera smoothing.
- Existing player movement controls.
- Any camera-related gameplay abilities.

Make the zoom transition smooth rather than allowing the camera to jump suddenly between distances.

**Camera collision and visibility:**

Ensure the camera works correctly when zoomed far out.

Inspect:
- Terrain clipping.
- Building obstruction.
- Camera collision.
- Map boundaries.
- Units disappearing due to visibility settings.
- Excessive object pop-in.
- Incorrect camera positioning.
- UI scaling and readability.

The camera should not become stuck inside geometry when zooming in or out.

Do not simply increase the camera's distance variable without checking its other constraints.

The player should be able to zoom out far enough to gain a useful battlefield overview while still being able to identify important units and threats.

Keep the existing camera behavior at normal distances unchanged.

