34. Test transitions between exploration and combat.
35. Test transitions between different boss encounters.
36. Test situations involving multiple bosses.
37. Verify that music does not overlap unexpectedly.
38. Confirm that music volume does not overpower gameplay audio.
39. Verify that downloaded tracks work without an internet connection.
40. Confirm that all music licenses and attribution requirements have been checked.

Do not mark any feature as complete merely because its interface, animation, or visual effect appears to work. Verify the actual underlying gameplay behavior.

The final result should deliver more challenging and intelligent boss encounters, destructible but extremely durable squad-protection armor, improved battlefield awareness, and a genuinely skill-based combat mechanic that rewards precision and tactical thinking.

Most importantly, every boss should feel like a unique threat, with its own teleportation behavior, combat identity, and recognizable musical theme. The update should make encounters more suspenseful, strategic, and memorable without sacrificing the existing game's performance or core gameplay systems.